X - run without cartridges››Syntax:› X [/C] [/L mode] [d:][path]file[.ext]›   [params]››Runs a program with all cartridges›switched off, including the DOS›cartridge, for programs that need the›RAM there (e.g. Turbo BASIC XL). The›DOS library is then not available:›only plain binary files run,›single-byte I/O is slow and›redirection is limited. Rule: if a›program fails with a cartridge›present, run it with X.››Options:› /C  clear $80-$FF, $400-$6FF and›     MEMLO to MEMTOP before loading› /L  loading mode as for LOAD››Example:› X TURBO.COM››See also: LOAD, CAR, BASIC›